      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "andreas@roughedge.se",
        "date": "2026-11-21T12:55:59Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(post): read the declared rotary-before-traverse order of a post\n\ntormach.cps turns A at the safe Z before each section's first X/Y\ntraverse, so the posed law over-read it and refused legal microARC 4\nprograms (tilt_a180_routes, tilt_basis0_edited_file). A post now\ndeclares that order (rotariesBeforeTraverse = true); the posed law then\nreads the operation at its own pose. Every other post reads the strict\nway. A user's own declaring script gets a note on the path, the stamp\nfollows the declaration, and posting_rotaries_first.rs pins the real\nTormach order. The first-4axis-part restamp is dropped: its stamps are\nas on main again.\n\nRefs #3100\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
